⚡ EXEC DISCIPLINE: run any `python3 <path>` command exactly as written — a bare invocation, nothing appended, no shell wrapping, no chaining with other commands, no output redirection, no exit-code capture. Scripts always print one JSON line to stdout with a `status` field (ok/error/degraded); parse that final line to decide what to do. openclaw 2026.4.11 rejects complex shell invocations before they run. Check for upcoming meetings needing alerts. Run gcal-fetch.py for events in the next 2 hours. Filter to real meetings starting in 15-45 minutes. Read sent-alerts.json to skip already-alerted meetings. For any un-alerted meeting: check cache for existing prep, generate if missing via meeting-prep.py. Send Telegram: '🐷🔍 Heads up — meeting in {N} min
📋 {Title}
👥 {Attendees}
🎯 {Top bullets}
📌 {Open items}'. Record in sent-alerts.json. If no meetings approaching, return EXACTLY the empty string (zero bytes, no narration — not even "NO output", "Done", "all clear", or a status summary). Any text you emit is logged and charges tokens even when no Telegram message is sent. Write result to ~/.openclaw/meetings-coach-workspace/cache/last-pre-meeting.json as JSON: {"timestamp": "<ISO UTC>", "meetings_alerted": <N>, "status": "ok" | "error", "summary": "<one sentence>"}. DO NOT touch ~/Dropbox/openclaw-backup/agents/meetings-coach.status.md — the heartbeat cron owns that file.
